<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <%- include("./partials/head.ejs") %>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles/texty.css" />
</head>
<body>
    <header>
        <%- include("./partials/navbar.ejs") %>
    </header>
    <main>
        <section>
            <h1>Pregame</h1>
            <p>
                Tictactoe is a two player game.
                The first person to enter a room is assigned the X and the other player is assigned an O. In the case
                that there is just one person within the room, he becomes the room leader. The room leader always goes
                first (no matter his sign).
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>
                Game Objective
            </h1>
            <p>
                The aim of the game is to form a straight line with your specific letter or sign first. This means you must prevent
                an opponent from forming one before you do. Lines can either be horizontal, vertical or along the diagonals of the board.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>On My turn?</h1>
            <p>
                Click or tap on an empty square to place your sign within it. A square already occupied cannot be reused.
                After placing a sign, your turn is over and you must wait for your opponent to make a move.
            </p>
        </section>
        <section>
            <h1>When does it end?</h1>
            <p>
                The game ends when a straight line is made by one of the players as described or if there are no more empty spaces.
                The game can then be restarted by the room leader.
            </p>
        </section>
    </main>
    <script>
            // definition of variables
            const showNavbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarDropdownButton");
            const navbarLine = document.getElementById("navbarLine");
            const navbarActions = document.getElementById("navbarActions");
            const mediaQuery = window.matchMedia("(max-width: 760px)");
            
            let isNavbarToggled = false;

            // toggle navbar dropdown on or off
            showNavbarActions.addEventListener("click", () => {
                isNavbarToggled = !isNavbarToggled;
                if (isNavbarToggled) {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25B2;";
                } else {
                    navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden";
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                }
            });
            function handleMediaChange(e) {
                navbarLine.className = "navbar-line hidden";
                isNavbarToggled = false;
                if (e.matches) {
                    showNavbarActions.innerHTML = "&#x25BC;";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions hidden"
                    showNavbarActions.className = "";
                } else {
                    showNavbarActions.className = "hidden";
                    navbarActions.className = "navbar-actions"
                }
            }
            mediaQuery.addEventListener("change", e => handleMediaChange(e))
            handleMediaChange(mediaQuery);
    </script>
</body>

</html>
